              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nAPPEAL,CLOSED,REF_EVENTS ONLY (NEFs),RMM\n\nU.S. District Court\nSouthern District of Florida (West Palm Beach)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 9:24-cr-80053-AMC All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Mcintosh Date Filed: 04/16/2024\n\nMagistrate judge case numbers: 9:24-mj-08152-BER Date Terminated: 07/23/2025\n9:24-mj-08274-WM\n\nAssigned to: Judge Aileen M. Cannon\nReferred to: Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe\n\nDefendant (1)\nKeith Duane Mcintosh represented by Richard Aldo Serafini\n18306-050 Serafini Law Office, LLC\nYOB: 1959; English 100 SE Third Avenue, Suite 2210\nTERMINATED: 12/20/2024 Fort Lauderdale, FL 33394\n754-223-4718\nFax: 800-535-9913\nEmail: ras@rserafinilaw.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\nSEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN Imprisonment: 40 Years to run consecutively with Count 2s.\n(1s) Supervised Release: Life.\nACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL\nImprisonment: 15 Years to run consecutively with Count 1s.\nCONSTITUTING/CONTAINING CHILD PORNO\nSupervised Release: Life.\n(2s)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:2251(d) and (e) - SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF\nCHILDREN Dismissed.\n(1)\n18:2252A(a)(2) and (b)(1) - ACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL\nCONSTITUTING/CONTAINING CHILD PORNO Dismissed.\n(2)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\n18:2251.F Conspiracy to advertise child pornography\n\nAssigned to: Judge Aileen M. Cannon\nReferred to: Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe\nAppeals court case number: 25-12686-A USCA\n\nDefendant (2)\nThomas Peter Katsampes represented by John Patrick Musca\n19258-511 Mucsa Law\nOxford 800 SE 3rd Avenue\nFederal Correctional Institution Suite 200\nInmate Mail/Parcels Fort Lauderdale, FL 33316\nPost Office Box 1000 954-357-0797\nOxford, WI 53952 Email: john@muscalaw.com\nENGLISH; YOB:1973 TERMINATED: 08/18/2025\nTERMINATED: 07/23/2025 LEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nKimberly Acevedo\nRosenbaum & Acevedo, L.L.P.\nFL\n100 SE 2nd Street\nSuite 3400\n33131\nMiami, FL 33131\n305-446-6099\nFax: 305-675-6156\nEmail: ka@rosenbaumacevedolaw.com\nTERMINATED: 08/18/2025\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nPhilip Robert Horowitz\nPhilip R. Horowitz, Esq.\n9100 South Dadeland Boulevard\nSuite #1500\nMiami, FL 33156\n305-670-1915\nEmail: HorowitzDefense@aol.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nPending Counts Disposition\nSEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN IMPRISONMENT: 250 MONTHS. SUPERVISED RELEASE:\n(1s) LIFE.\nACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL\nIMPRISONMENT: 240 MONTHS. SUPERVISED RELEASE:\nCONSTITUTING/CONTAINING CHILD PORNO\nLIFE.\n(2s)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\n18:2251.F (18:2251(d) and (e))\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Gregory Schiller\nU.S. Attorney's Office\n500 S. Australian Ave.\nSuite 400\nWest Palm Beach, FL 33401\n954-789-6285\nEmail: gregory.schiller@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nKyle P. Reynolds\nU.S. Department of Justice\n1301 New York Avenue, NW Suite 1100\nWashington, DC 20005\n(202) 616-2842\nEmail: kyle.reynolds@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nMarx Calderon\nDOJ-USAO\n99 NE 4th Street\nMiami, FL 33132\n305-961-9036\nEmail: marx.calderon@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nWilliam G. Clayman\nU.S. Department of Justice\nCriminal Division\nChild Exploitation and Obscenity Section\n1301 New York Avenue, NW Suite 1100\nWashington, DC 20005\n(202) 514-0040\nEmail: william.clayman@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Retained\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n03/28/2024 1 CRIMINAL COMPLAINT as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1). (tmn) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/28/2024 Arrest of Keith Duane Mcintosh in Western District of Michigan. (mpl1) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/29/2024 SYSTEM ENTRY - Docket Entry 2 restricted/sealed until further notice. (tmn) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/29/2024 3 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Kyle P. Reynolds appearing for USA. . Attorney Kyle P. Reynolds added to party\nUSA(pty:pla). (Reynolds, Kyle) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 03/29/2024)\n03/29/2024 4 Rule 5(c)(3)/ Rule 40 Documents received from Western District of Michigan as to Keith Duane Mcintosh. (mpl1) [9:24-mj-08152-BER]\n(Entered: 03/29/2024)\n04/12/2024 5 NOTICE OF HEARING as to Keith Duane Mcintosh - Initial Appearance set for 4/15/2024 at 01:30 PM in Miami Division before MIA\nDuty Magistrate Judge. (spe) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 04/12/2024)\n04/15/2024 6 Minute Order for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Jonathan Goodman: Initial Appearance as to Keith Duane Mcintosh held on\n4/15/2024. Bond recommendation/set: Keith Duane Mcintosh (1) Government request Pretrial Detention. Date of Location Custody\n(Arrest or Surrender): 3/28/2024. Arraignment set for 4/29/2024 at 10:00 AM in the West Palm Beach Division before WPB Duty\nMagistrate Judge. Pretrial Detention Hearing set for 4/17/2024 at 10:00 AM in the West Palm Beach Division before WPB Duty\nMagistrate Judge. Preliminary Examination set for 4/29/2024 at 10:00 AM in the West Palm Beach Division before WPB Duty Magistrate\nJudge. Attorney added: Richard Aldo Serafini for Keith Duane Mcintosh for Criminal CJA representation. Date attorney was appointed\nCJA: 4/15/2024. (Digital JG-13:41:57; 13:53:37)\n\nIt is ORDERED AND ADJUDGED that pursuant to the Due Process Protections Act, the Court confirms the United States obligation to\ndisclose to the defendant all exculpatory evidence- that is, evidence that favors the defendant or casts doubt on the United States case, as\nrequired by Brady v. Maryland, 373 U.S. 83 (1963) and its progeny, and ORDERS the United States to do so. The government has a duty\nto disclose any evidence that goes to negating the defendants guilt, the credibility of a witness, or that would reduce a potential sentence.\nThe defendant is entitled to this information without a request. Failure to disclose exculpatory evidence in a timely manner may result in\nconsequences, including, but not limited to, exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings,\ndisciplinary action, or sanctions by the Court. Signed by Magistrate Judge Jonathan Goodman on 4/15/2024. (fbn) [9:24-mj-08152-BER]\n(Entered: 04/15/2024)\n04/16/2024 7 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Detention Hearing by Keith Duane Mcintosh. Responses due by 4/30/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Text of\nProposed Order)(Serafini, Richard) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 04/16/2024)\n04/16/2024 8 PAPERLESS ORDER granting 7 Motion to Continue Detention Hearing as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1). Detention Hearing reset for\n4/19/2024 at 10:00 AM in West Palm Beach Division before WPB Duty Magistrate Judge. Signed by Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe\non 4/16/2024. (spe) [9:24-mj-08152-BER] (Entered: 04/16/2024)\n04/16/2024 9 INDICTMENT as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1) count(s) 1, 2 w/forfeiture. (spe) (Additional attachment(s) added on 4/16/2024: # 1\nRestricted Unredacted Indictment) (spe). (Entered: 04/16/2024)\n04/16/2024 10 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE William G. Clayman appearing for USA. . Attorney William G. Clayman added to party\nUSA(pty:pla). (Clayman, William) (Entered: 04/16/2024)\n04/18/2024 11 Joint MOTION to Continue Detention Hearing by Keith Duane Mcintosh. Responses due by 5/2/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Text of\nProposed Order)(Serafini, Richard) (Entered: 04/18/2024)\n04/19/2024 12 PAPERLESS Minute Order for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe: Status Conference re: Detention as to Keith\nDuane Mcintosh held on 4/19/2024. ARRAIGNMENT as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1) Count 1,2 held on 4/19/2024. Defendant present\nwith counsel. Government requested pre-trial detention; the Defendant stipulated to pretrial detention with the right to revisit at a later\ndate. Defendant is to be detained; no detention hearing held. Written order to be issued. Defense confirmed defendant's understanding of\ncharges and maximum penalties. Defendant waived formal reading of the Indictment, entered a plea of not guilty, demanded a jury trial\nand requested the standing discovery order be issued. Total time in court: 4 minutes. Attorney Appearance(s): Marc Osborne (AUSA);\nRichard Aldo Serafini (CJA). (Digital 10:28:32)\n\nPAPERLESS STANDING DISCOVERY ORDER: The defendant(s) having been arraigned this date in open Court, it is Ordered that\nwithin 14 days of the date of this order that all parties to this action shall review and comply with Southern District of Florida Local Rules\n88.10 (Criminal Discovery), and 88.9(c) (Motions in Criminal Cases). Upon a sufficient showing, the Court may at any time, upon a\nproperly filed motion, order that the discovery or inspection provided for by this Standing Order be denied, restricted or deferred, or make\nsuch other order as is appropriate. It is expected by the Court, however, that counsel for both sides shall make a good faith effort to\ncomply with the letter and spirit of this Standing Order. It shall be the continuing duty of counsel for both sides to immediately reveal to\nopposing counsel all newly discovered information or other material within the scope of Local Rule 88.10. Signed by Magistrate Judge\nRyon M. McCabe on 4/19/2024. (spe) (Entered: 04/19/2024)\n04/19/2024 13 PAPERLESS ORDER denying as moot 11 Motion to Continue as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1). Signed by Magistrate Judge Ryon M.\nMcCabe on 4/19/2024. (spe) (Entered: 04/19/2024)\n04/19/2024 14 ORDER OF DETENTION as to Keith Duane Mcintosh. Signed by Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe on 4/19/2024. See attached\ndocument for full details. (ls) (Entered: 04/19/2024)\n04/19/2024 15 OMNIBUS ORDER Setting Trial Date and Establishing Pretrial Instructions and Sentencing Procedures as to Keith Duane Mcintosh. In\nLimine Motions due by 5/10/2024. Motions due by 5/10/2024. Calendar Call set for 5/28/2024 01:45 PM in Fort Pierce Division before\nJudge Aileen M. Cannon. Jury Trial set for 6/3/2024 in Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. Signed by Judge Aileen M.\nCannon on 4/19/2024. See attached document for full details. (ls)\n\nPattern Jury Instruction Builder - To access the latest, up to date changes to the 11th Circuit Pattern Jury Instructions go to\nhttps://pji.ca11.uscourts.gov or click here. (Entered: 04/19/2024)\n05/03/2024 16 Joint MOTION for Protective Order by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh. Responses due by 5/17/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Stipulation for\nProtective Order, # 2 Text of Proposed Order)(Schiller, Gregory) (Entered: 05/03/2024)\n05/03/2024 17 First RESPONSE to Standing Discovery Order by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Schiller, Gregory) (Entered: 05/03/2024)\n05/06/2024 18 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Marx Calderon appearing for USA. As to Forfeiture. Attorney Marx Calderon added to party\nUSA(pty:pla). (Calderon, Marx) (Entered: 05/06/2024)\n05/07/2024 19 ORDER granting in part and denying in part 16 Unopposed Motion for Protective Order and Entering Protective Order as to Keith Duane\nMcintosh (1). Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 5/7/2024. See attached document for full details. (ls) (Entered: 05/08/2024)\n05/10/2024 20 SPEEDY TRIAL REPORT by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Clayman, William) (Entered: 05/10/2024)\n05/10/2024 21 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial by Keith Duane Mcintosh. Responses due by 5/24/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed\nOrder)(Serafini, Richard) (Entered: 05/10/2024)\n05/10/2024 22 ORDER granting 21 Unopposed Motion to Continue Trial as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1). In Limine Motions due by 8/6/2024. Motions\ndue by 8/6/2024. Calendar Call set for 10/1/2024 01:45 PM in Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. Jury Trial set for\n10/7/2024 in Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 5/10/2024. See attached\ndocument for full details. (ls) (Entered: 05/10/2024)\n05/24/2024 23 Second RESPONSE to Standing Discovery Order by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Schiller, Gregory) (Entered: 05/24/2024)\n05/31/2024 24 SPEEDY TRIAL REPORT by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Clayman, William) (Entered: 05/31/2024)\n06/06/2024 1 CRIMINAL COMPLAINT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes (1). (swr) [9:24-mj-08274-WM] (Entered: 06/06/2024)\n06/06/2024 SYSTEM ENTRY - Docket Entry 2 restricted/sealed until further notice. (swr) [9:24-mj-08274-WM] (Entered: 06/06/2024)\n06/06/2024 3 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Kyle P. Reynolds appearing for USA. . Attorney Kyle P. Reynolds added to party\nUSA(pty:pla). (Reynolds, Kyle) [9:24-mj-08274-WM] (Entered: 06/06/2024)\n06/07/2024 Arrest of Thomas Peter Katsampes in District of Minnesota. (mpl1) [9:24-mj-08274-WM] (Entered: 06/12/2024)\n06/12/2024 4 Rule 5(c)(3)/ Rule 40 Documents received from District of Minnesota as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. (mpl1) [9:24-mj-08274-WM]\n(Entered: 06/12/2024)\n06/21/2024 25 SPEEDY TRIAL REPORT by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Clayman, William) (Entered: 06/21/2024)\n07/09/2024 26 SUPERSEDING INDICTMENT as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1) count(s) 1s, 2s, Thomas Peter Katsampes (2) count(s) 1s, 2s;\nFORFEITURE (tmn) (Additional attachment(s) added on 7/9/2024: # 1 Restricted Unredacted Indictment) (tmn). (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/09/2024 27 NOTICE OF HEARING as to Thomas Peter Katsampes Initial Appearance set for 7/10/2024 10:00 AM in West Palm Beach Division\nbefore WPB Duty Magistrate Judge. (tmn) (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/10/2024 28 PAPERLESS Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Bruce E. Reinhart: Initial Appearance as to Thomas Peter\nKatsampes held on 7/10/2024. Date of Arrest or Surrender: 7/10/2024. Defendant was present/sworn. Defendant was advised of the\ncharges, rights and possible maximum penalties. Defendant advised the Court that he has retained counsel. The Court continued the Initial\nappearance hearing to allow defendant's counsel to be available. (Continuation of Initial Appearance set for 7/11/2024 10:00 AM in West\nPalm Beach Division before WPB Duty Magistrate Judge.) Total time in court: 6 minutes. Attorney Appearance(s): AUSA Gregory\nSchiller (Digital 10:13:50) (tmn) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/11/2024 29 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: John Patrick Musca appearing for Thomas Peter Katsampes . Attorney John Patrick Musca\nadded to party Thomas Peter Katsampes(pty:dft). (Musca, John) (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/11/2024 30 PAPERLESS Minute Order for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Bruce E. Reinhart: Initial Appearance and ARRAIGNMENT as\nto Thomas Peter Katsampes (2) Count 1s,2s held on 7/11/2024. Date of Arrest or Surrender: 7/11/2024. Defendant was present with\ncounsel. Defense counsel filed a permanent appearance. PTD hearing held and defendant detained by the D/MN. Defendant waived formal\nreading of the Superseding Indictment, entered a plea on not guilty, demanded a trial by jury and requested the Court issue the Standing\nDiscovery Order. The Court issued the Due Process Protections Act order. Total time in court: 6 minutes. Attorney Appearance(s):\n(AUSA) Emily Walters, (RETAINED) John Patrick Musca (Digital 10:12:30)\n\nIt is ORDERED AND ADJUDGED that pursuant to the Due Process Protections Act, the Court confirms the United States obligation to\ndisclose to the defendant all exculpatory evidence- that is, evidence that favors the defendant or casts doubt on the United States case, as\nrequired by Brady v. Maryland, 373 U.S. 83 (1963) and its progeny, and ORDERS the United States to do so. The government has a duty\nto disclose any evidence that goes to negating the defendants guilt, the credibility of a witness, or that would reduce a potential sentence.\nThe defendant is entitled to this information without a request. Failure to disclose exculpatory evidence in a timely manner may result in\nconsequences, including, but not limited to, exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings,\ndisciplinary action, or sanctions by the Court.\n\nPAPERLESS STANDING DISCOVERY ORDER: The defendant(s) having been arraigned this date in open Court, it is Ordered that\nwithin 14 days of the date of this order that all parties to this action shall review and comply with Southern District of Florida Local Rules\n88.10 (Criminal Discovery), and 88.9(c) (Motions in Criminal Cases). Upon a sufficient showing, the Court may at any time, upon a\nproperly filed motion, order that the discovery or inspection provided for by this Standing Order be denied, restricted or deferred, or make\nsuch other order as is appropriate. It is expected by the Court, however, that counsel for both sides shall make a good faith effort to\ncomply with the letter and spirit of this Standing Order. It shall be the continuing duty of counsel for both sides to immediately reveal to\nopposing counsel all newly discovered information or other material within the scope of Local Rule 88.10. Signed by Magistrate Judge\nBruce E. Reinhart on 7/11/2024. (tmn) (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/11/2024 31 OMNIBUS ORDER SETTING TRIAL DATE AND ESTABLISHING PRETRIAL INSTRUCTIONS AND SENTENCING\nPROCEDURES as to Keith Duane Mcintosh, Thomas Peter Katsampes. In Limine Motions due by 8/6/2024. Pretrial Motions due by\n8/6/2024. Calendar Call set for 10/1/2024 01:45 PM in Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. Jury Trial set for 10/7/2024\nin Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 7/11/2024. See attached document for full\ndetails. (jas)\n\nPattern Jury Instruction Builder - To access the latest, up to date changes to the 11th Circuit Pattern Jury Instructions go to\nhttps://pji.ca11.uscourts.gov or click here. (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/12/2024 32 SPEEDY TRIAL REPORT by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (Clayman, William) (Entered: 07/12/2024)\n07/22/2024 33 Agreed MOTION for Protective Order by USA as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 8/5/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Stipulation\nas to Protective Order, # 2 Text of Proposed Order)(Schiller, Gregory) (Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/22/2024 34 First RESPONSE to Standing Discovery Order by USA as to Thomas Peter Katsampes (Schiller, Gregory) (Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/22/2024 35 PAPERLESS ORDER OF REFERRAL TO MAGISTRATE JUDGE as to Keith Duane McIntosh. Pursuant to 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 636 and the\nMagistrate Rules of the Local Rules of the Southern District of Florida, this matter is hereby referred to United States Magistrate Judge\nRyon M. McCabe for Change of Plea Hearing to take all necessary and proper action as required by law and/or to submit a Report and\nRecommendation to this Court regarding the Change of Plea by Defendant, Keith Duane McIntosh. The parties shall submit via email to\nJudge Ryon M. McCabe's chambers a stipulated factual proffer and any written plea agreement in Word prior to the scheduled change of\nplea hearing. Please note the calendar call and jury trial are cancelled for this defendant Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 7/22/2024.\n(tci) (Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/26/2024 36 ORDER granting in part 33 Motion for Protective Order and Entering Modified Protective Order as to Keith Duane McIntosh as to\nThomas Peter Katsampes (2). Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 7/26/2024. See attached document for full details. (drz) (Entered:\n07/26/2024)\n07/29/2024 37 NOTICE OF HEARING as to Keith Duane Mcintosh - Change of Plea Hearing set for 8/15/2024 at 02:00 PM in Courtroom 3, 4th Floor,\nWest Palm Beach Division before Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe. (spe) (Entered: 07/29/2024)\n07/31/2024 38 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Kimberly Acevedo appearing for Thomas Peter Katsampes . Attorney Kimberly Acevedo\nadded to party Thomas Peter Katsampes(pty:dft). (Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered: 07/31/2024)\n07/31/2024 39 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 8/14/2024. (Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered:\n07/31/2024)\n08/01/2024 40 PAPERLESS ORDER denying without prejudice 39 Defendant's Motion to Continue Trial as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. The Motion\ndoes not indicate Defendant's position with respect to the Speedy Trial Act. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 8/1/2024. (tci)\n(Entered: 08/01/2024)\n08/01/2024 41 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 8/15/2024. (Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered:\n08/01/2024)\n08/02/2024 42 ORDER GRANTING DEFENDANT'S UNOPPOSED MOTION TO CONTINUE TRIAL - Ends of Justice as to Thomas Peter\nKatsampes Time excluded from 08/01/2025 until 01/13/2025. Re: 41 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial . ( In Limine Motions due by\n11/1/2024., Calendar Call set for 1/7/2025 01:45 PM before Judge Aileen M. Cannon., Jury Trial set for 1/13/2025 in Fort Pierce Division\nbefore Judge Aileen M. Cannon.) - Motions terminated: 41 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial filed by Thomas Peter Katsampes.\nSigned by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 8/2/2024. See attached document for full details. (drz) (Entered: 08/02/2024)\n08/02/2024 43 SPEEDY TRIAL REPORT by USA as to Keith Duane Mcintosh, Thomas Peter Katsampes (Clayman, William) (Entered: 08/02/2024)\n08/14/2024 44 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: Kimberly Acevedo appearing for Thomas Peter Katsampes (Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered:\n08/14/2024)\n08/15/2024 45 PAPERLESS Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe: Change of Plea Hearing as to Keith Duane\nMcintosh held on 8/15/2024. Keith Duane Mcintosh (1) Guilty Count 1s,2s. Defendant remanded into USM custody. Total time in court:\n43 minutes. Attorney Appearance(s): Gregory Schiller (AUSA); Richard Aldo Serafini (CJA). (D