lliam) (Entered: 10/03/2024)\n10/08/2024 56 DRAFT Disclosure of Presentence Investigation Report of Keith Duane Mcintosh. This is a limited access document. Report access\nprovided to attorneys Kyle P. Reynolds, William G. Clayman, Gregory Schiller, Marx Calderon, Richard Aldo Serafini by USPO\n(Attachments: # 1 Position of Parties)(Roman, Milagros) (Entered: 10/08/2024)\n10/28/2024 57 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial and Extend Pretrial Deadlines by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 11/12/2024.\n(Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered: 10/28/2024)\n10/29/2024 58 PAPERLESS ORDER denying without prejudice Defendant Katsampes's Second Motion to Continue Trial 57 . Defendant Katsampes\npreviously moved for, and obtained, a three-month continuance of trial in this case and almost a three-month extension of the deadline to\nfile pre-trial motions 41 42 . Defendant Katsampes now moves again for a continuance of both deadlines, referring to a digital forensic\nreport and a need for additional time \"to explore a plea resolution to this matter\" 57 . Upon review of the Motion and the full record, the\nCourt is not satisfied that a second lengthy continuance is warranted in this case. Any future motion for a continuance of any deadline shall\ninclude particularized facts and justification for the relief requested, along with a clear waiver of speedy trial rights by the Defendant\nhimself, for the specified period. All deadlines remain in full force and effect. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 10/29/2024. (tci)\n(Entered: 10/29/2024)\n10/30/2024 59 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial and Extend Pretrial Deadlines by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 11/13/2024.\n(Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered: 10/30/2024)\n11/01/2024 60 ORDER GRANTING IN PART RENEWED SECOND MOTION TO CONTINUE CALENDAR CALL, TRIAL, AND PRETRIAL\nMOTIONS DEADLINE - Ends of Justice as to Thomas Peter Katsampes Time excluded from 10/30/2024 until 01/27/2025. Re: 59\nUnopposed MOTION to Continue Trial and Extend Pretrial Deadlines. ( In Limine Motions due by 11/20/2024., Motions due by\n11/20/2024., Calendar Call set for 1/21/2025 01:45 PM before Judge Aileen M. Cannon., Jury Trial set for 1/27/2025 in Fort Pierce\nDivision before Judge Aileen M. Cannon.) - Motions terminated: 59 Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial and Extend Pretrial\nDeadlines filed by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 11/1/2024. See attached document for full details.\n(drz) (Entered: 11/01/2024)\n11/04/2024 61 MOTION to Continue Sentencing Hearing by Keith Duane Mcintosh. Responses due by 11/18/2024. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed\nOrder)(Serafini, Richard) (Entered: 11/04/2024)\n11/05/2024 62 FINAL Addendum 1 Disclosure of Presentence Investigation Report of Keith Duane Mcintosh. This is a limited access document. Report\naccess provided to attorneys Kyle P. Reynolds, William G. Clayman, Gregory Schiller, Marx Calderon, Richard Aldo Serafini by USPO\n(Attachments: # 1 Addendum)(Weisberg, Frances) (Entered: 11/05/2024)\n11/05/2024 63 PAPERLESS ORDER granting 61 Defendant's Motion to Continue Sentencing Hearing as to Keith Duane McIntosh. The sentencing\nhearing is rescheduled to December 19, 2024, at 10:30 AM in the Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. If more than 30\nminutes is needed, counsel shall file a notice no later than December 12, 2024, estimating the amount of time needed and specifying the\nnumber of witnesses to be called. Objections to the PSI are due on or before 11/15/2024. All sentencing memoranda shall be filed on or\nbefore 12/8/2024. Counsel please note the change to your files. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 11/5/2024. (tci) (Entered:\n11/05/2024)\n11/12/2024 64 PAPERLESS NOTICE OF CHANGE OF PLEA HEARING as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. Change of Plea Hearing set for 1/7/2025\n02:30 PM in Fort Pierce Division before Judge Aileen M. Cannon. The parties shall submit via email to cannon@flsd.uscourts.gov a\nstipulated factual proffer a