 sentencing. The Court orders Probation to file a revised PSI regarding paragraph 36. Defendant's factual objection is\notherwise denied. Defendant sentenced to 55 years' imprisonment followed by lifetime supervised release, with a $200.00 special\nassessment. The term of imprisonment consists of 40 years' imprisonment as to Count 1 and 15 years' imprisonment as to Count 2. Terms\nto run consecutive. Mandatory and special conditions imposed. Defendant advised of right to appeal.Total time in court: 1 hour(s). Court\nReporter: Laura Melton, 772-467-2327 / Laura_Melton@flsd.uscourts.gov. (tci) (Entered: 12/19/2024)\n12/20/2024 73 JUDGMENT as to Keith Duane Mcintosh (1), Count(s) 1, 2, Dismissed.; Count(s) 1s, Imprisonment: 40 Years to run consecutively with\nCount 2s. Supervised Release: Life.; Count(s) 2s, Imprisonment: 15 Years to run consecutively with Count 1s. Supervised Release: Life.\nAssessment: $200.00 Closing Case for Defendant. - Motions terminated: 67 MOTION for a Downward Variance filed by Keith Duane\nMcintosh. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 12/20/2024. See attached document for full details. (drz) Modified text on 12/20/2024\n(drz). (Entered: 12/20/2024)\n12/23/2024 74 MOTION to Appoint of Public Defender by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 1/6/2025. (drz) (Entered: 12/23/2024)\n12/23/2024 75 PAPERLESS ORDER OF REFERRAL TO MAGISTRATE JUDGE as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. Pursuant to 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 636 and the\nMagistrate Rules of the Local Rules of the Southern District of Florida, the Motion to Appoint Public Defender 74 is hereby referred to\nUnited States Magistrate Judge Ryon M. McCabe for appropriate disposition according to law. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on\n12/23/2024. (tci) (Entered: 12/23/2024)\n01/08/2025 76 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION in case as to Thomas Peter Katsampes 74 MOTION to Appoint Counsel : Motion Hearing set for\n1/13/2025 10:00 AM in Fort Pierce Division before Magistrate Judge Shaniek Mills Maynard (mab) (Ent