is is a limited\naccess document. Report access provided to attorneys Kyle P. Reynolds, William G. Clayman, Marx Calderon, John Patrick Musca,\nKimberly Acevedo by USPO (Attachments: # 1 Addendum)(Roman, Milagros) (Entered: 07/22/2025)\n07/22/2025 104 PAPERLESS ORDER and MINUTE ENTRY for proceedings held before Judge Aileen M. Cannon: Sentencing held on 7/22/2025 as to\nThomas Peter Katsampes. Witness FBI Special Agent Drew Steinmetz sworn and testified. The Court reviewed and received into evidence\na psycho-sexual evaluation and various victim impact statements. The psycho-sexual evaluation shall be filed under seal and remain\nsealed. The victim impact statements shall also be filed under seal at least temporarily, subject to the United States' request for leave to\npermanently seal such items. Defendant to file additional character letter on the docket. The Court adopts the Pre-Sentence Investigation\nReport in full with a factual revision as stated on the record. Defendant sentenced to 250 months' imprisonment as to Count 1 and 240\nmonths' imprisonment as to Count 2, to run concurrently; followed by supervised release for a term of Life as to Counts 1 and 2, all such\nterms to run concurrently; with a $200.00 special assessment, a $10,000.00 JVTA Assessment, and $23,000.00 in restitution (pursuant to\nstipulation). Defendant waives restitution hearing. Mandatory and special conditions imposed. Defendant advised of right to appeal. Total\ntime in court: 2 hours and 15 minutes. Attorney Appearances: Kyle P. Reynolds, William G. Clayman, John Patrick Musca, and Kimberly\nAcevedo. Additional Appearance: Frances Weisberg, USPO. Court Reporter: Laura Melton, 772-467-2327 /\nLaura_Melton@flsd.uscourts.gov. (sm1) (Entered: 07/23/2025)\n07/22/2025 105 STIPULATION REGARDING RESTITUTION by USA, Thomas Peter Katsampes as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. (sm1) (Entered:\n07/23/2025)\n07/22/2025 106 ORDER GRANTING AGREED MOTION FOR RESTITUTION 105 AND ADOPTING JOINT STIPULATION REGARDING\nRESTITUTION as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 7/22/2025. See attached document for full details.\n(sm1) (Entered: 07/23/2025)\n07/23/2025 107 JUDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes (2), Count(s) 1s, IMPRISONMENT: 250 MONTHS. SUPERVISED RELEASE: LIFE.;\nCount(s) 2s, IMPRISONMENT: 240 MONTHS. SUPERVISED RELEASE: LIFE. Restitution: $23,000.00 Assessment: $200.00 JVTA\nAssessment: $10,000. Closing Case for Defendant. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 7/23/2025. See attached document for full\ndetails. (cwc) (Entered: 07/23/2025)\n07/29/2025 SYSTEM ENTRY - Docket Entry 108 restricted/sealed until further notice. (kpe) (Entered: 07/29/2025)\n08/05/2025 109 NOTICE OF APPEAL re DE 107 Judgment by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Filing fee $ 605.00. IFP Filed. Within fourteen days of the filing\ndate of a Notice of Appeal, the appellant must complete the Eleventh Circuit Transcript Order Form regardless of whether transcripts are\nbeing ordered [Pursuant to FRAP 10(b)]. For information go to our FLSD website under All Forms and look for Transcript Order Form\nwww.flsd.uscourts.gov/forms/all-forms. (Acevedo, Kimberly) Modified text on 8/6/2025 to create docket entry relationship (apz).\n(Entered: 08/05/2025)\n08/05/2025 110 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney and Motion to Proceed in Forma Pauperis by Kimberly Acevedo and John P. Musca for / by Thomas\nPeter Katsampes. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Acevedo, Kimberly) (Entered: 08/05/2025)\n08/05/2025 111 Clerk's Notice to Filer re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment. Document Not Linked; ERROR - The filed document was not linked to\nthe related docket entry. The correction was made by the Clerk. It is not necessary to refile this document. (apz) (Entered: 08/06/2025)\n08/06/2025 Transmission of Notice of Appeal, Judgment under appeal, and Docket Sheet as to Thomas Peter Katsampes to US Court of Appeals re\n109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment, Notice has been electronically mailed. (apz) (Entered: 08/06/2025)\n08/06/2025 112 Unopposed MOTION to Seal Victim Impact Statements, see 104 by USA as to Thomas Peter Katsampes. Responses due by 8/20/2025.\n(Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Clayman, William) (Entered: 08/06/2025)\n08/06/2025 113 PAPERLESS ORDER granting 112 United States' Unopposed Motion to Seal Victim Impact Statements as to Thomas Peter Katsampes\n(2). The Court agrees under the particular circumstances presented that shielding the subject information from public view is warranted\nand hereby orders the sealing of such items until further Court order. Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 8/6/2025. (AMC) (Entered:\n08/06/2025)\n08/07/2025 114 Acknowledgment of Receipt of NOA from USCA as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment, date received\nby USCA: 8/6/2025. USCA Case Number: 25-12686-A. (apz) (Entered: 08/08/2025)\n08/18/2025 115 ORDER Granting 110 Motion to Proceed in Forma Pauperis on Appeal; Granting Motion to Withdraw as Retained Counsel; and\nAppointing Federal Public Defender as Appellate Counsel. Kimberly Acevedo and John Patrick Musca withdrawn from case as to Thomas\nPeter Katsampes (2). Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 8/18/2025. See attached document for full details. (apz) (Entered:\n08/19/2025)\n11/18/2025 117 NOTICE/Request for Status of the Appointment of Attorney to Assist with Appeal by Thomas Peter Katsampes. (A copy of DE 115 Order\nand case docket sheet has been mailed to Thomas Peter Katsampes.) (apz) (Entered: 11/19/2025)\n11/19/2025 116 CLERK'S NOTICE for FPD-WPB as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 115 Order on Motion to Withdraw as Attorney. Additional Notice of\nElectronic Filing (NEF) sent to FPD (FPD) (apz) (Entered: 11/19/2025)\n04/10/2026 118 MOTION to Appoint Counsel and for Issuance of a CJA voucher for Transcripts Only by Thomas Peter Katsampes. Attorney Philip\nRobert Horowitz added to party Thomas Peter Katsampes(pty:dft). Responses due by 4/24/2026. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit USCA Order\nof Appointment)(Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/10/2026)\n04/13/2026 119 ORDER granting in part DE 118 DEFENDANT'S MOTION TO APPOINT COUNSEL SOLELY TO ORDER TRANSCRIPTS FOR\nAPPEAL as to Thomas Peter Katsampes (2). Signed by Judge Aileen M. Cannon on 4/13/2026. See attached document for full details.\n(cwc) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/14/2026 120 TRANSCRIPT ORDER FORM as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, filed by Thomas Peter\nKatsampes. Transcript Requested. Counsel/Party submitting transcript order form: Philip R. Horowitz, Esquire. Link to Circuit Transcript\nOrder Form PDF sent to: Court Reporter Coordinator. Payment Status: Completed CJA 24. (Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/14/2026 121 TRANSCRIPT ORDER FORM as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, filed by Thomas Peter\nKatsampes. Transcript Requested. Counsel/Party submitting transcript order form: Philip R. Horowitz, Esquire. Link to Circuit Transcript\nOrder Form PDF sent to: Court Reporter Coordinator. Payment Status: Completed CJA 24. Digitial/DAR file name(s): (Digital\n10:13:24) (Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/14/2026 122 TRANSCRIPT ORDER FORM as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, filed by Thomas Peter\nKatsampes. Transcript Requested. Counsel/Party submitting transcript order form: Philip R. Horowitz, Esquire. Link to Circuit Transcript\nOrder Form PDF sent to: Court Reporter Coordinator. Payment Status: Completed CJA 24. Digitial/DAR file name(s): (Digital\n10:07:28) (Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/14/2026 123 TRANSCRIPT ORDER FORM as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, filed by Thomas Peter\nKatsampes. Transcript Requested. Counsel/Party submitting transcript order form: Philip R. Horowitz, Esquire. Link to Circuit Transcript\nOrder Form PDF sent to: Court Reporter Coordinator. Payment Status: Completed CJA 24. Digitial/DAR file name(s): (Digital\n14:09:37) (Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/14/2026 124 TRANSCRIPT ORDER FORM as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, filed by Thomas Peter\nKatsampes. Transcript Requested. Counsel/Party submitting transcript order form: Philip R. Horowitz, Esquire. Link to Circuit Transcript\nOrder Form PDF sent to: Court Reporter Laura Melton,. Payment Status: Completed CJA 24. (Horowitz, Philip) (Entered: 04/14/2026)\n04/16/2026 125 COURT REPORTER ACKNOWLEDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, 124 Circuit\nTranscript Order Form,. Court Reporter: Laura Melton, 772-467-2327 / Laura_Melton@flsd.uscourts.gov. Estimated filing date of\ntranscript 5/13/2026. USCA number 25-12686. (Melton, Laura) (Entered: 04/16/2026)\n04/28/2026 126 COURT REPORTER ACKNOWLEDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 120 Circuit Transcript Order Form. Court Reporter:\nStephen Franklin, 561-313-8439. Estimated filing date of transcript 5/24/2026. (apz) (Entered: 05/01/2026)\n04/28/2026 127 COURT REPORTER ACKNOWLEDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 121 Circuit Transcript Order Form. Court Reporter:\nStephen Franklin, 561-313-8439. Estimated filing date of transcript 5/24/2026. (apz) (Entered: 05/01/2026)\n04/28/2026 128 COURT REPORTER ACKNOWLEDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 122 Circuit Transcript Order Form. Court Reporter:\nStephen Franklin, 561-313-8439. Estimated filing date of transcript 5/24/2026. (apz) (Entered: 05/01/2026)\n04/28/2026 129 COURT REPORTER ACKNOWLEDGMENT as to Thomas Peter Katsampes re 123 Circuit Transcript Order Form. Court Reporter:\nStephen Franklin, 561-313-8439. Estimated filing date of transcript 5/24/2026. (apz) (Entered: 05/01/2026)\n05/07/2026 130 TRANSCRIPT of Sentencing as to Thomas Peter Katsampes held on 7/22/2025 before Judge Aileen M. Cannon, 1-117 pages, re: 109\nNotice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, Court Reporter: Laura Melton, 772-467-2327 / Laura_Melton@flsd.uscourts.gov. USCA Case\nNumber: 25-12686. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or purchased by contacting the Court Reporter/Transcriber\nbefore the deadline for Release of Transcript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER. Redaction Request due\n5/28/2026. Redacted Transcript Deadline set for 6/8/2026. Release of Transcript Restriction set for 8/5/2026. (Melton, Laura) (Entered:\n05/07/2026)\n05/07/2026 131 TRANSCRIPT NOTIFICATION as to Thomas Peter Katsampes - Transcript(s) ordered on: 4/14/2026 by Philip Horowitz, Esq. has/have\nbeen filed by Court Reporter: Laura Melton, 772-467-2327 / Laura_Melton@flsd.uscourts.gov re 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,,\n124 Circuit Transcript Order Form,. (Melton, Laura) (Entered: 05/07/2026)\n05/28/2026 132 TRANSCRIPT of Motion Hearing as to Thomas Peter Katsampes held on 1/13/2025 before Magistrate Judge Shaniek Mills Maynard, 1-\n10 pages, re: 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment, Court Reporter: Stephen Franklin, SFranklinUSDC@aol.com. Transcript may be\nviewed at the court public terminal or purchased by contacting the Court Reporter/Transcriber before the deadline for Release of\nTranscript Restriction. After that date it may be obtained through PACER. Redaction Request due 6/18/2026. Redacted Transcript\nDeadline set for 6/29/2026. Release of Transcript Restriction set for 8/26/2026. (apz) (Entered: 05/29/2026)\n05/28/2026 133 TRANSCRIPT NOTIFICATION as to Thomas Peter Katsampes - Transcript ordered on: 4/14/2026 by Philip R. Horowitz, Esq. has been\nfiled by Court Reporter: Stephen Franklin, SFranklinUSDC@aol.com re 127 Court Reporter Acknowledgment. (apz) (Entered:\n05/29/2026)\n05/28/2026 134 TRANSCRIPT of Motion Hearing as to Thomas Peter Katsampes held on 1/17/2025 before Magistrate Judge Shaniek Mills Maynard, 1-4\npages, re: 109 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment, Court Reporter: Stephen Franklin,\nSFranklinUSDC@aol.comStephen_Franklin@cand.uscourts.gov